    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The build is green. Full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded a derived `telephoneDisplay` field that formats the stored E.164 `telephone` for humans while leaving raw `telephone` untouched.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `telephoneDisplay` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the new field.\n\n2. **`E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 made the class `public` and added a `display(String e164)` method: splits off the country code (recognized code, else up to 3 leading digits), then emits `+<code> <national digits grouped in threes>`. Non-E.164 / null input is returned verbatim so every stored owner stays renderable.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` invoking `E164Telephone.display(owner.getTelephone())`, alongside the other derived-field expressions.\n\nFor the test's input `0412 345 678`, the pipeline normalizes to `+61412345678` (raw `telephone`) and the mapper renders `+61 412 345 678` (`telephoneDisplay`) \u2014 matching `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay`.",
